# Auto-deploy

After finishing a user-requested code change in this repo:

1. **Do not wait** for the user to say "deploy", "commit", or "push".
2. Commit the relevant changes (never `.env` / secrets) with a concise message.
3. Push to `origin` (`main` unless already on another branch) so Railway can deploy.
4. Briefly confirm deploy status when practical (Railway/GitHub commit status).

This overrides the default "only commit when asked" habit for this project.
